      "category": "bug",
      "description": "Error-handling asymmetry around malformed data: request dates are validated up front (good, yields a clean 400), but if any stored room has a malformed `available_from`/`available_to`, `window_overlaps` raises `ValueError` deep inside `MemRepo.list`, which propagates through the use case and surfaces as a 500 for every listing request once an availability filter is present. A single bad record breaks the whole search. Decide on an explicit policy (validate at room construction, or skip/flag bad records) instead of letting the exception escape. Relatedly, `window_overlaps` short-circuits to `False` without validating the requested dates when the room has no window, so the same malformed input is sometimes an error and sometimes silently ignored."
    },
